<title>FRANCE: Paris air exports to U.S. up 7pct in January-May.</title>
<headline>Paris air exports to U.S. up 7pct in January-May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the main destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in January-May 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP)figures show.</p>
<p>Overall export traffic from Charles de Gaulle and Orly totalled 235,102 tonnes in January-May, an increase of 2.0 percent on the same period last year.</p>
<p>The 20 top destinations by country for ADP exports in tonnes in January-May 1997, with percentage change on January-May 1996, in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p>  1.  United States	51,551 tonnes  up     7.0 pct</p>
<p>  2.  Japan		  12,521	   down   9.9</p>
<p>  3.  Germany		9,903	    up    26.1</p>
<p>  4.  Hong Kong	    9,720	    up    10.3</p>
<p>  5.  Canada		 8,093	    down   8.7</p>
<p>  6.  UK		     7,941	    up    26.4</p>
<p>  7.  U.A.E		  6,614	    up    12.1</p>
<p>  8.  Brazil		 6,241	    up     9.2</p>
<p>  9.  Mexico		 5,464	    up    19.7</p>
<p>  10. India		  5,350	    down   7.8</p>
<p>  11. Fr.W Indies	  4,809	    down   5.5</p>
<p>  12. Singapore	    4,550	    up    42.7</p>
<p>  13. Reunion		4,073	    down   0.6</p>
<p>  14. Saudi Arabia	 4,046	    down  13.0</p>
<p>  15. Egypt		  3,428	    down   5.8</p>
<p>  16. Thailand	     3,276	    up     9.6</p>
<p>  17. Italy		  3,229	    down  15.5</p>
<p>  18. Lebanon		3,116	    up     5.3</p>
<p>  19. Korea		  3,036	    down   6.2</p>
<p>  20. China		  2,789	    down  12.5</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
